  "question": {
    "text": "If the distance between the first maxima and fifth minima of a double slit pattern is $7 \\mathrm{~mm}$ and the slits are separated by $0.15 \\mathrm{~mm}$ with the screen 50 $\\mathrm{cm} .$ from the slits, then the wavelength of the light used is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7Mtpl",
      "text": "$200 \\mathrm{nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HVhzM",
      "text": "$100 \\mathrm{nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yDkDg",
      "text": "$800 \\mathrm{nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6Ik3L",
      "text": "$600 \\mathrm{nm}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "There are three and a half fringes from first maxima to fifth minima as shown.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/DHk5IdcNhRtbsrgLZt9dkQBjUw9Nsh1MBaP3byDVApE.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$\\Rightarrow \\beta=\\frac{7 \\mathrm{~mm}}{3.5}=2 \\mathrm{~mm} \\Rightarrow \\lambda=\\frac{\\beta \\mathrm{D}}{\\mathrm{d}}=600 \\mathrm{nm}$",
    "image": null
  },
